# The choice rule of the HM baseline's judgments, a module of its own that a
# type check opts into: a choice of two members, each judged, (x_0 ∥ x_2 + x_0)
# and (x_1 ∥ x_3 + x_1), is judged by the unify node of the two members' types
# and its own type, type_of of the choice, written as the choice of the choice
# and its parallel with them: both are top up to contextual equivalence, and the
# judgment is the choice by absorption, as the application rule's is
# (hindley_milner_unions_application). So that a group of values written
# `(m1 + … + mk) ∥ T`, which the JIT holds as one storage, is a type the
# e-graph's HM reaches for a choice of typed values.
